<title>UK: ITG set to become Ireland's first DCM issue.</title>
<headline>ITG set to become Ireland's first DCM issue.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent Telecoms Group (ITG) said on Thursday it planned to become the first company to float on the newly formed Developing Companies Market (DCM) of the Irish Stock Exchange on May 2.</p>
<p>The company's shares will also be floated on the London Stock Exchnage's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on the same day.</p>
<p>ITG has raised about two million stg via a placing at 148 per share (IR156p), valuing the company at 6.75 million stg.</p>
<p>The company is one of the largest communications service providers in Ireland and said it had identified a number of significant new opportunities.</p>
<p>--Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
</text>
